#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065281} :activity/id #uuid "5c56a3ff-c078-5460-97b4-4cf59ad749b8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050719 :topic/id #uuid "61178d17-c292-5e1d-a08e-a6ce03bd5a13" :topic/math-academy-id 330} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065281 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065416 :tutorial/content "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers. \n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(+)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2.$\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)},$ the result is going to be negative:\n![](images/b6/b64108fa03fc286ddcd04ac4cd7a9d77c1672d0ced66ebb1953c97afa5488533.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs: $6 \\div 2 = 3.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3 }.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b92ac2e4-b983-5fd5-bc18-7dfb821497f0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8108 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "39aa10e9-422a-5c1c-b5b2-de119dcca067" :step/math-academy-id 77819 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065282}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065282 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064357 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063941 :question/id #uuid "5b4f3b5f-2f0b-5178-9055-cf83a9885920" :question/math-academy-id "e-12972"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b434d0d5-bd04-554b-888e-df84e3961839" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049349}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064489} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064564} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064764} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442926} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442927} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442933} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442937}] :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Negative Number by a Positive Number"} :step/id #uuid "46d3cb51-86b4-59d6-8a39-eab709bb05a3" :step/math-academy-id 77820 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065283}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065283 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065417 :tutorial/content "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(+)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2),$ we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}.$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/79/797eda7126fff569fccda2681c628f99f103057d7c5e23c1b65cb566b48ef203.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs: $8 \\div 2 = 4.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "67beb927-7da4-5576-8982-1a823c878691" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8109 :tutorial/title "The Quotient of a Positive and a Negative is a Negative"} :step/id #uuid "b2792086-a352-5ca3-b086-f381a58864aa" :step/math-academy-id 77824 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065284}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065284 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064358 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063942 :question/id #uuid "166aaac7-bc88-577a-8e84-47347408e3c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12973"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de4234d-932f-537c-9eae-746e1711cccd" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064490} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064551} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442925} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442929} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442934} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442938}] :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Positive Number by a Negative Number"} :step/id #uuid "503ce197-02ae-5ae2-897a-80af7de15a2a" :step/math-academy-id 77825 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065285}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065285 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065418 :tutorial/content "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3).$ We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](images/d3/d31776de6ab95f8178d0bdd6e3b34cfa2f4fc0b987851dcace50aff1818936da.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs: $12 \\div 3 = 4.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b1d3d95e-7953-5c5b-b97b-d4eb85e1f80d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8111 :tutorial/title "The Quotient of a Negative and a Negative is a Positive"} :step/id #uuid "b129822d-f637-5611-9cad-e2f8b6aefca4" :step/math-academy-id 77828 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065286}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065286 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064359 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063943 :question/id #uuid "e2005c9d-c0ff-5b8e-bc64-4e222fd19fdf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12976"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b85ef92b-d5fb-5927-aa68-60e72d0b3e72" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050287}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064491} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064549} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064763} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442930} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442931} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442936}] :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Negative Number by a Negative Number"} :step/id #uuid "8ddc832d-59f9-5fa2-85e2-002f7b9c4ccc" :step/math-academy-id 77829}] :activity/title "Dividing With Negative Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186064421}]}
